  "_doc": "Weapon action one-shots. src is relative to the extracted Tactical Shooter Pack (C:/tb/audio-src/tsp/Tactical Shooter Pack). t = approximate time of the CONTACT transient in the source (snapped to the real transient, +-12 ms); dur = seconds kept after it -- chosen from the source's onset map so a slice never swallows the next, louder event of the pack's own (longer) animation. lead_ms = extra source kept BEFORE the contact (slide / approach scrape of pump and bolt strokes); the manifest records the resulting anchor_ms and the engine starts the file at (contact time - anchor_ms). Other optional fields: pitch (semitones), gain_db, eq [[kind,hz,gain_db,q]], hp/lp (Hz), fade_in_ms, snap (false for noise-like cloth), preroll_ms (default 3). Draw/holster variants: t0..main = cloth lead varispeed-fitted to main_at_ms so the thud lands on the animation's arrival; thud = extra layer {src,t,dur,pitch,delay_ms,gain_db} dropped in at delay_ms. synth = procedural one-shot (build_elements.py).",
